# ResonantOS 2.0.0 Alpha — Environment Variables for addon SDK testing.
#
# This file is documentation only. It is not loaded automatically; copy the
# variables you need into your shell environment before running the test
# scripts.
#
# The tests documented in INSTALL.md (deepseek-harness:smoke,
# test:external-agent-runtime, test:phase35) DO NOT require any of these
# environment variables. They run entirely in-process and use the
# Cordis stub at examples/fixtures/cordis-stub.mjs.
#
# Set the variables below only if you are wiring the real DeepSeek API
# instead of the stub.

# DeepSeek API key. Required only if you are talking to real DeepSeek
# (not the in-repo stub). The dispatcher does NOT read this directly;
# the Cordis-kernel runtime does. Set it in the shell that launches
# Cordis, not in this shell.
#
# Obtain from: https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# Example: export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="sk-..."
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# DeepSeek Harness / Cordis HTTP endpoint. Defaults to
# `http://127.0.0.1:3080`. Override only if you are running Cordis on
# a non-default port or remote host.
#
# The addon manifest's `service.entrypoint` reads this default. Set
# this if you want the dispatcher's `service.entrypoint` to point at
# a non-default URL when you regenerate the manifest for a real
# install.
# DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_ENTRYPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:3080

# Force the dispatcher to use the in-repo Cordis stub instead of any
# real remote endpoint. The stub lives at
# `examples/fixtures/cordis-stub.mjs`. Default if unset: real Cordis.
#
# Set to "1" only when you want to override the manifest's
# `service.entrypoint` at dispatch time without rewriting the manifest.
# This is mostly used by integration tests; production callers should
# leave it unset.
# DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_MODE=stub
